                                                "sense_id": "fca09ee1-58c6-304d-aed9-411501d21987",
                                                "text": "The Ambassador warned him of the consequences if his mission to Moscow were a failure, both to Churchill's position at home and to Russia's prospects in the war. He insisted that he should not allow himself to be offended 'by a peasant who didn't know any better'. Churchill listened in silence, then returned to the dacha leaving Clark Kerr outside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
